---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
---

<Layout title="FAQ">
  <section class="faq">
    <h1 class="label">// faq</h1>
    <dl>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>
          <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">
            &gt;
          </span>
          HotMess?
        </dt>
        <dd>
          I hiked the <a href="https://www.pcta.org">Pacific Crest Trail</a> in
          2010. On a long trail, it's a tradition to adopt an alter ego (a trail
          name). My propensity for misplacing things landed me the title of
          'HotMess'.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <dt>
          <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">
            &gt;
          </span>
          What's with the masthead?
        </dt>
        <dd>
          If you work with JavaScript, you've probably encountered the famous{" "}
          <a href="https://www.destroyallsoftware.com/talks/wat">wat talk</a>,
          detailing some of JavaScript's best... eccentricities. I'm so enamored
          with the masthead expression (which evaluates to true in JS), that I'm
          considering getting a tattoo of it.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .faq {
    margin-top: 56px;
  }
  dl {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
  }
  .item {
    padding: 24px 0;
  }
  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .prompt {
    margin-right: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
  }
  dd a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
